Z||000006||Alex4mula||04-05-2000||04:52 PM||||I was just curious becasue there is another topic mentioning that you may be able to use the stock 2.8 injectors with a 3.4 motor. I was talking to Ed Parks on Daytona and he told me that I could do that also with a fuel preassure regulator. I'm just hours away of ordering my 3.4 and want to know if I really need to budget for new injectors. I was wondering that if your stock injectors work OK with nitro why can't they work OK with a 3.4.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||04-05-2000||05:38 PM||||You can easily fool an injector in thinking it bigger than it really is by upping the pressure via adjustable fuel pressure regulator.  I wouldn't recommend large pressure increases, but 5-10 psi of more fuel pressure could easily be done with very little side effects.  Now if you go 20-30 psi more, then you will proably be looking into driveability problems.  Injector changes can only be accomplished on a Fiero from changing the computer calibration because of its 'speed density' nature.  If it were a 'mass air' nature, then it just needs the mass air meter to be recalibrated for the certain sized injectors (like the 89-93 5.0's)<BR> ||||reg||1
